Description: Ansible deployments from Slack, with an encrypted variable store
 hoisty runs Ansible playbooks from Slack or a web interface. Every variable,
 SSH deploy key and API token lives in a SQLCipher database that only a
 human-typed passphrase opens.
 .
 The daemons start locked and hold nothing until an administrator runs
 "hoisty unlock" on the machine, so no passphrase is ever stored on disk and a
 stolen disk image yields nothing. Deploy targets, their groups and their pinned
 SSH host keys are kept per project.
 .
 The whole install lives under /var/lib/hoisty. The program and its vendored
 virtualenv are root-owned and read-only to the service account, so a playbook
 that goes bad cannot rewrite the program that is next handed the passphrase.
